      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their cited evidence. The E7 claim about 55% less tax is sourced from Resolution Foundation via contractoruk.com (an advocacy-adjacent site), but the Resolution Foundation is the primary source and is institutional-grade; acceptable. E6 and E9 are both projected/estimated costs and are correctly tiered as 'projected'. The rationale is evidence-driven, does not impute motive, and is party-blind. The direction 'worsens' is supported by multiple claims pointing to material revenue loss (~\u00a32bn/year) with no funded offset in the policy text. The countervailing argument (indirect boost to contractor activity) is acknowledged but correctly noted as unquantified. Magnitude 'moderate' and horizon 'this-parliament' are plausible given the annual cost estimates. No tier blurring, no lever leakage, no false balance issues detected."
